                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Gave it a lot of chances, just not worth the time and effort to put into a sub-par game that is missing a lot of what makes a CRPG good. The limited amount of enemies to fight and finite amount of resources you can find in the game, not to mention how choked you are on currency to do anything worthwhile (if you spend gold on gear you can't spend it on the trainers, and you need both but you can't).\r\n\r\nYou also can't customize your characters in a way that satisfies because no matter what you're missing a lot. You can at most have 3 skills that you're working towards on any given character but even THAT is too many skills and you'll always feel like you're lagging behind against even rats, crabs, and seagulls.\r\n\r\nAlso RNG can bite you in the butt too, if you need 'seagull skin' for a wolfkin's pelt quest, if you didn't luck out in the rng combined with getting foraging up high enough (which involves making your combat skills worse so you're hobbling yourself in the long run) you're likely not gonna get the drops you need for the quest - and remember, the enemies are finite meaning if you killed all the seagulls and they didn't drop enough pelts? Too bad, that quest is bricked on your save.\r\n\r\nI love CRPGs, and there's stuff in this game I love, but do yourself a favor and give it a pass.\r\n\r\nP.S. Even the modding scene is abysmal, people have looked into it and the only things they can tweak is dialogue-based, you can't even mod the game with fun stuff. Sad.",
